    },
    {
      "component": "Computed oscillation",
      "description": "A pinned study driven by the product's real numbers.",
      "prompt": "Take the product's published frequency and derive everything from it: beats elapsed against running time, the swing angle as a sine of scroll progress scaled to the stated amplitude, and an amplitude that decays realistically across the stated reserve. Redraw the arc from the current amplitude each frame so the drawn sweep and the printed figure are the same value. Never animate the hand on a timer — bind it to scroll so it reads in both directions."
